# PRIMARY (protocol-level) timings -- the headline adaptor-overhead table #
##########################################################################
--- COMPUTATION, TIER 1: CORE CRYPTO (struct API; pure computation, no codec)
    (per op: microseconds AND cycles, each mean +/- sample SD) ---

 Shared (public params pp=(A,H); KeyGen -> pk=t, sk=r):
   Setup             79.34 +/-   1.74 us       285067 +/-      6241 cyc
   KeyGen            67.73 +/-   0.65 us       243346 +/-      2351 cyc

 Base path (simplified Dilithium-style, c = H(pk, w, M); no t'):
   Sign             492.25 +/-  10.90 us      1768750 +/-     39151 cyc
   Verify           134.40 +/-   3.78 us       482928 +/-     13590 cyc

 LAS adaptor path (statement t' folded into the hash, c = H(pk, w+t', M)):
   PreSign          508.13 +/-  19.85 us      1825781 +/-     71341 cyc
   PreVerify        141.48 +/-   5.17 us       508344 +/-     18590 cyc
   Adapt            145.36 +/-   3.31 us       522301 +/-     11884 cyc
   Ext               58.00 +/-   0.19 us       208388 +/-       673 cyc

 Adaptor overhead (adaptor op vs the base op it mirrors; core tier, us):
   PreSign       vs Sign       508.13 vs   492.25   (+3.2%)
   PreVerify     vs Verify     141.48 vs   134.40   (+5.3%)
   Adapt         vs Verify     145.36 vs   134.40   (+8.2%)
   Ext (separate)               58.00            (no base analogue)

--- COMPUTATION, TIER 2: END-TO-END PACKED (byte API: validating unpack ->
    core -> pack INSIDE the call -- the boundary upstream sign.c exposes;
    same repetition scheme and units; Setup has no packed twin) ---

 Shared:
   KeyGen_packed      206.15 +/-   1.17 us       740745 +/-      4214 cyc

 Base path (bytes in/out):
   Sign_packed        841.94 +/-  11.87 us      3025259 +/-     42646 cyc
   Verify_packed      471.49 +/-  11.90 us      1694131 +/-     42772 cyc

 LAS adaptor path (bytes in/out; las_verify_packed = the on-chain-style entry):
   PreSign_packed     959.07 +/-  23.34 us      3446102 +/-     83858 cyc
   PreVerify_packed   600.71 +/-   6.47 us      2158443 +/-     23254 cyc
   Adapt_packed       809.64 +/-  12.76 us      2909181 +/-     45832 cyc
   Ext_packed         613.53 +/-   2.08 us      2204530 +/-      7472 cyc

 Adaptor overhead at the packed boundary (adaptor op vs base op, us):
   PreSign_packed   vs Sign_packed      959.07 vs   841.94   (+13.9%)
   PreVerify_packed vs Verify_packed    600.71 vs   471.49   (+27.4%)
   Adapt_packed     vs Verify_packed    809.64 vs   471.49   (+71.7%)
   Ext_packed (separate)                613.53            (no base analogue)
   NOTE: these packed-boundary overheads fold in EXTRA CODEC WORK, not just
   adaptor math -- PreSign_packed/PreVerify_packed additionally decode the
   pk-sized statement t'; Adapt_packed additionally decodes t' and the witness
   r' and re-packs the adapted signature.  The CORE tier above isolates the
   pure adaptor computation (the headline overhead); the codec-cost table
   below prices the byte boundary itself.

 Codec boundary cost (packed minus core, per op, us -- the price of the
 byte boundary: validating unpack of the inputs + pack of the output;
 differences of independently measured means, so small values sit within
 the SDs above):
   KeyGen_packed    - KeyGen        +138.43   (+204.4%)
   Sign_packed      - Sign          +349.69   ( +71.0%)
   Verify_packed    - Verify        +337.08   (+250.8%)
   PreSign_packed   - PreSign       +450.94   ( +88.7%)
   PreVerify_packed - PreVerify     +459.23   (+324.6%)
   Adapt_packed     - Adapt         +664.28   (+457.0%)
   Ext_packed       - Ext           +555.54   (+957.9%)

