--- B. ADAPT TIMING CLARIFICATION (microseconds, mean +/- SD) ---
   Adapt checked total       145.361 +/-  3.308   (PROTOCOL: las_adapt above, incl. internal PreVerify)
   witness-add only            4.141 +/-  0.074   (DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: z=z_hat+r'; not a protocol op)
   A real Adapt MUST pre-verify first; the witness-add line is a lower bound,
   not a usable operation.  Use 'Adapt checked total' for protocol cost.

--- C. COMMUNICATION (packed bytes; BYTE-LEVEL only, NOT EVM gas) ---
   public key    pk = t                5888
   secret key    sk = r                 960
   statement     Y = t'               5888   (64.1% of the signature; t' has pk size)
   witness       r'                    960   (same packed layout as sk = r)
   challenge     c_tilde                64   (H digest; FIPS 204 lambda/4 for this set)
   response      z (final)            9120   (99.3% of the signature)
   response      z_hat (pre-sig)      9120   (same packed layout as z)
   signature         (c, z)           9184
   pre-signature     (c, z_hat)       9184   (same size as the signature)
   final adapted sig (c, z)           9184   (an ordinary signature)
   commitment    w = A*y            internal computed commitment; hashed into c; not transmitted
   -- protocol-component catalogue (context; what each object is / why counted or not) --
   pp=(A,H)  A' seed                    32   (public params; only this 32-byte seed is transmitted)
   pp=(A,H)  expanded A'             41216   (n*ell polys; DERIVED from the seed, NOT transmitted)
   y (signing mask, S_gamma)         9120   (n+ell polys; INTERNAL, hashed into c via w, NOT transmitted)
   w = A*y (commitment)              5888   (n polys; INTERNAL, hashed into c, NOT transmitted)
   pi (NIZK well-formedness proof)    n/a   (paper-level off-chain proof; NOT implemented / NOT measured)
   tx metadata (addrs/amounts/nonces) excl   (application/ledger layer; EXCLUDED from this accounting)
   atomic-swap payload (byte-level only):
     off-chain   = Y + 2*pre-signature        =  24256   [= t' + 2*(c, z_hat)]
     settlement  = 2*signature                =  18368   [= 2*(c, z)]
     settlement incl. escrowed Y = Y + 2*sig  =  24256
   (EVM/keccak gas for on-chain verification is a separate axis; see evm/.)

--- D. COMPONENT MICROBENCHMARKS (microseconds, mean +/- SD) ---
   Cost-attribution ESTIMATES timing LOCAL COPIES of the inner steps
   (behaviourally identical to las.c) -- NOT the protocol entry points above.
   A-product / commitment w = A*y                         54.400 +/-  0.374
   challenge hash  c = H(pk, w(+t'), M)                   47.287 +/-  0.310
   NTT(s)  (n+ell polys; ONCE PER CALL, hoisted)          23.522 +/-  0.084
   NTT(c)  (one poly; once per attempt / per verify)       1.563 +/-  0.023
   c*r  (one poly; pointwise+invNTT, operands pre-NTT'd)   2.496 +/-  0.032
   c*r  per attempt (NTT(c) + n+ell pointwise+invNTT)     39.013 +/-  0.029
   norm check  |z|inf over n+ell polys                     1.794 +/-  0.022
   w + t'   (n polys)                                      4.209 +/-  0.007
   z_hat + witness r'   (n+ell polys)                      4.141 +/-  0.074
   c*t  per verify (NTT(c) + n x (NTT(t)+pw+invNTT))      33.883 +/-  0.050
   KeyGen/Gen: sample r (n+ell ternary polys)              6.293 +/-  0.023
     (KeyGen = sample r + A*r; A*r is the A-product line above; statement Y gen = KeyGen)
   Ext: s = z - z_hat   (n+ell polys)                      4.040 +/-  0.016
   Ext: A*s   (recompute statement; = an A-product)       53.200 +/-  0.292
   Ext: t' == A*s check   (n polys)                        0.463 +/-  0.024
   note: a full Sign/PreSign attempt applies c*r across N_PLUS_ELL = n+ell = 15
         response polynomials; Verify-style challenge multiplication applies
         c*t across LAS_N = n = 8 public-key polynomials.  NTT hoisting
         follows upstream ref/sign.c: NTT(s) is paid once per CALL (amortised
         over ~e rejection attempts), NTT(c) once per attempt / per verify.

--- E. NORM-MARGIN DIAGNOSTICS (achieved infinity-norm vs the reject bound;
       max over the 2000 sampled accepted signatures from section A) ---
   accepted |z|inf      max    230340   vs accept limit g-k   =    230340   (100.00% of band)
   accepted |z^|inf     max    230339   vs accept limit g-k-1 =    230339   (100.00% of band)
   Interpretation: the RESPONSE z/z^ saturates its band (~100%) -- the bound is
   the binding constraint and is exactly why ~63% of attempts are rejected.
   Contrast the AMHL cumulative WITNESS ||s_j||inf, which is tiny (<=K) vs the
   g-k-K band: that bound is extremely loose (see bench_app, the K-series table).
